From 1b26f444be3ae8a773aab65d6aa62bbb0e07ebcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Bockelie <aaron@bockelie.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:26:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] hexagonrpcd: serve the sns_registry interface with a
 fixed property table

The Snapdragon Sensor Core calls remotectl_open("sns_registry") during
boot and then get_property() for Android system properties. On Android
libsns_registry_skel.so answers from property_get(). Without the
interface the DSP logs "Could not find local interface sns_registry" and
"Unsupported handle: 4294967295" on every boot.

The method layout comes from the stock SM8450 skeleton:

	long get_property(in sequence<char> prop_name,
			  rout sequence<char> prop_value);

Answer from a small table (ro.revision, ro.boot.hardware, ro.hardware,
ro.product.model, ro.product.device) and return an empty string for
unknown names, logging the requested name so the table can grow.
